WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
Hey everyone, привет, welcome to привет русский, episode 33, it's 3rd union 2006 года.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.220
I'm allia, and today we're going to learn some really fun Russian words.

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:10.700
Ready?

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.100
Поехали, that means let's go.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:18.860
Our word of the day is «кот», «кот», it sounds like «кот», and rhymes with «кот».

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:19.900
This word means cat.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:23.160
Think of «кот» as a cozy cat curled up on a cot.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:27.240
Repeat after me, «кот», «cause, «кот», now let's use it.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.200
Это мой кот.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.100
This means this is my cat.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.120
Let's build more animal words today.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:36.360
The first one is «сабака», «сабака», it means dog.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.700
У меня есть «сабака», this means I have a dog.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:43.360
«сабака» sounds like «со барка», which is perfect for a dog.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.400
Repeat after me, «сабака», «поз», «сабака».

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.860
Next comes «птица», «птица», this word means bird.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.240
«Птица летает», the bird flies.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:56.580
«Пти» sounds like «твит», because birds tweet.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:02.660
Repeat after me, «птица», «cause, «птица», now say «реба» with me.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.900
«Реба» — «Р-I-H-Па», it means fish.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.200
Реба плавает, the fish swims.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.760
Реба rhymes with «реба», so picture of funny rib-fish.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:15.780
Repeat after me, «реба», «поз», «реба».

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:19.200
Мит медведь next, медведь, медведь, this means bear.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.320
Медведь большой, the bear is big.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:25.220
«Мэк» sounds like «медл», because a bear wins the medal for biggest animal.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:29.160
Repeat after me, «медведь», «поз», «медведь».

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:32.800
Here is «заяц», «захьяц», it means hair or rabbit.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.060
«заяц» прыгает, the hair jumps.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:39.080
«заяц» sounds like «сэй», so the hair says «хай» with a jump.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:44.140
Repeat after me, «заяц», «поз», «заяц», try «лошать» now.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:47.260
«лошать», «лошать», this word means horse.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:49.440
«лошать» бежит, the horse runs.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:52.820
«лошать» sounds like «лошать», where the horse might live.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:57.340
Repeat after me, «лошать», «поз», «лошать», say «слон» with me.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.380
«слон», «слон», it means elephant.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:01.940
«слон» большой, the elephant is big.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.920
«слон» sounds slow and strong, just like an elephant.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:08.240
Repeat after me, «слон», «поз», «слон».

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:11.020
One more word is «птичьи», «птичьи».

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:13.400
This means birds like the adjective form.

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:15.400
«птичьи» – «дум», «берт-house.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.240
«птичьи» sounds like «твит-чьи», just like bird sounds.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:22.860
Repeat after me, «птичьи», «поз», «птичьи».

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:26.060
Russian nouns have genders that change small words like «май».

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.680
«Кот» is masculine, so we say «мой-кот»,

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.740
«сабака» is feminine, so we say «майя-сабака».

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:33.740
English keeps my the same for everything.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:37.100
Russian gives every noun its own tiny label instead.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.440
In Russia, many families keep cats and dogs as pets.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.060
Neighbors often leave food for stray cats near apartment buildings.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:48.520
Russian also loves folk tales about bears as wise but grumpy characters.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:51.600
Now here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:54.220
Want to know a secret about «сабака»?

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.740
Did you know that «сабака» and the English word dog

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:59.160
are not related at all?

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:02.460
«сабака» actually shares an ancient route with words

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:03.620
from Persian and Turkish.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.460
This word began in old Iranian languages,

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:09.860
moved through Turkic tongues and reached Russian centuries ago.

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.300
Be careful though, because it can act like a false friend

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.840
in some other Slavic languages,

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.000
where similar sounds mean «гард» instead.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.680
Next time you see a dog, remember its long journey across Asia with «сабака»?

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.760
That story is your secret shortcut to remembering the word forever.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.700
Do you remember what «кот» means?

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.620
Try saying «эта-мой-кот» three times today.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:33.460
For kids, draw your favorite animal and say its Russian name out loud

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:34.800
three times while pointing.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.080
For adults, practice «эта» followed by the animal name

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.900
the next time you see a pet or picture.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.020
Молодец, that means well done.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.720
Remember, every expert started as a beginner.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:46.740
Practice saying today's words out loud,

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.860
even just once, and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:51.040
See you next time.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:52.400
«Пока», that's Russian 4.

00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:52.860
Bye!

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.440
This episode used AI voice synthesis of my voice.

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:59.280
Editorial selection and analysis are my own.
